List, add, remove or choose registry sources

Usage: shield registry [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     List effective registry sources
  add      Enroll a local directory or signed HTTPS registry, after confirmation
  remove   Remove a registration, preserving installed policy, after confirmation
  default  Choose the source for future unqualified search and add, after confirmation
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>
          Select a project; otherwise discover the nearest enrolled ancestor

      --scope <SCOPE>
          Affect this project's sources or the user's sources for every project

          Possible values:
          - project: This project
          - user:    Every project of the current user

          [default: project]

      --json
          Print one JSON result; commands that change policy refuse JSON mode

      --debug-log-dir <DEBUG_LOG_DIR>
          Write private per-process diagnostics in this directory (also `SHIELD_DEBUG_LOG_DIR`)

      --no-debug-log
          Disable diagnostic logging, including automatic debug-build logs

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          Compiled cache location for init, MCP setup or cache preparation

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
